QWinUI3 — dual licensing
==========================

QWinUI3 is **not** under a single license for the whole tree. Pick the terms that
match the modules you ship:

| Module | QML import | License | File |
|--------|------------|---------|------|
| **Theme** | `QWinUI3.Theme` | **MIT** | [LICENSE-MIT](LICENSE-MIT) |
| **Style** | `QtQuick.Controls` style `QWinUI3` | **MIT** | [LICENSE-MIT](LICENSE-MIT) |
| **Platform** | `QWinUI3.Platform` | **MIT** | [LICENSE-MIT](LICENSE-MIT) |
| **Compat** | (internal Qt shims) | **MIT** | [LICENSE-MIT](LICENSE-MIT) |
| **Extras** | `QWinUI3.Extras` | **GPL-3.0-or-later** | [LICENSE-GPL](LICENSE-GPL) / [COPYING](COPYING) |
| **Gallery** | demo app | **GPL-3.0-or-later** | [LICENSE-GPL](LICENSE-GPL) / [COPYING](COPYING) |

**MIT stack** — design tokens, Fluent Quick Controls styling, window bootstrap /
`StandardWindow` shells. You may use these in proprietary apps under MIT terms.

**GPL stack** — composites and product controls in **Extras** (NavigationView,
DataTable, charts/gauges, CommandPalette, RichEdit, on-screen keyboard chrome,
etc.) and the **Gallery** demo. If you link or import **Extras**, your app must
comply with **GPL-3.0** (source offer, license notice, same license on
derivatives).

Full consumer guide: [docs/licensing.md](docs/licensing.md).

Third-party vendored code keeps its upstream license (e.g. Keyman Core **MIT** in
`third_party/keyman/`).
